course: dictionary
lesson: 263
title: Amazed and amaze
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Amazed means very surprised, often in a happy way, because something is wonderful or hard to believe. «The boy was left shouting at nobody and looked silly, Jake's mates were amazed.» The mates were so surprised they could hardly believe what they had seen.
explain: Amazed is also the past form of amaze. Amaze, amazes, amazed and amazing all come from the same word. Ask yourself: did something surprise someone greatly? If it did, amazed is the right word.
explain: Use the words around amazed as clues. «Hooke's book Micrographia amazed readers with huge drawings of fleas and lice.» The clue is huge drawings: the readers were surprised by how big and detailed the pictures were. Swap in very surprised and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Amazed often comes before a small word: amazed at, amazed by, amazed that, amazed to see. «I'm amazed» is a short way of saying you cannot quite believe it.
fact: Amazed means very surprised, often in a happy way.
fact: «Amazed» is also the past form of «amaze», so it tells you that something surprised someone in the past.
fact: Wonder means being amazed and curious at the same time.
fact: Amazed is often followed by at, by, that or to: «amazed at», «amazed by», «amazed that», «amazed to see».
fact: «Otter leaps up from the shallows with an amazed and joyous bark» shows that amazed can mean surprised and happy at once.
exercise: «Hooke's book Micrographia amazed readers with huge drawings of fleas and lice.» What does amazed mean here? | Angry about the price | Bored by long words | Tired from reading | *Very surprised
exercise: What is the past form of amaze? | amazes | *amazed | amazing | amaze
exercise: «I'm amazed» means what? | I am bored and want to go home | *I cannot believe how wonderful or surprising it is | I am hungry | I have lost my bag
test: Fill the gap with the right word: «The crowd was ___ by the fireworks.» | sleepy | angry | bored | *amazed
test: In «Wonder means being amazed and curious at the same time», what does amazed mean? | Hungry | *Very surprised, often in a happy way | Tired | Angry
exam: «They row Portly back, set him down on the tow-path near the ford, and watch him waddle off until Otter leaps up from the shallows with an amazed and joyous bark.» What does amazed show about Otter? | Cross and rude | *Surprised and happy | Lost | Sleepy
